# SINGLE-OWNER SUB-PLACE NEG — THE KEYING CELL. The gate keys on the OUTERMOST
# PROJECTION, not on whether a container appears anywhere in the chain. `v[0].f`
# is outermost a `FieldAccess`, so a read THROUGH a container IS in scope and
# rejects; a BARE index place (`v[0]`) is not and does not.
#
# This cell exists because "INDEX places are deferred" reads as "reads out of
# containers are deferred", and that is false. Without it the suite's scope claim
# would be wrong in the direction that hides coverage nobody knows they have.
#
# The named omitted cell is the BARE index place only (`v[0]`, `d[k]`) —
# todo/t1225, deferred behind the owner's callee-borrow ruling (2026-09-04).
#
# CELL: type=Callable · place=field THROUGH an index (`v[0].f`) · position=bind.
# RED at 7bf11017e: `gg check` ACCEPTED (rc 0).
# ggdef: ABSTAIN (todo/t1227).

struct Holder:
    Callable[int()] f

Callable[int()] mk(int n):
    return (): n + 1

void main():
    Vector[Holder] v = []
    v.push(Holder(mk(40)))
    Callable[int()] g = v[0].f
    print(g())
